  "overview": "**PatternFly** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#0066cc` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `redhatdisplay` with `redhattext` body copy (36px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and stepped `#ffffff` -> `#f2f2f2` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **Red Hat**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/patternfly/patternfly-react#readme), repo https://github.com/patternfly/patternfly-react, package `@patternfly/react-tokens`, frameworks: react, css. Inventory: **91** colors, **49** typography steps, and **16** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 16 component tokens with documented paddings: `10px 18px`, `9px 13px`, `18px 20px`, `4px 10px`, `10px 16px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f2f2f2` cards; separate sibling sections using `#e0e0e0` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#ffffff` -> `#f2f2f2`) and `1px solid #e0e0e0` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#0066cc` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#0066cc` with `#f7f7f8` text (5.2:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `redhatdisplay` headings with `redhattext` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f2f2f2` surface shifts and `#e0e0e0` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-default` fields and secondary buttons."
